        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "Fundus pulverulentus is a rare form of patterned dystrophy of the retinal pigment epithelium characterized by a granular appearance in the macula with coarse and punctiform mottling of the retinal pigment epithelium within the macular region. Association with choroidal neovascularization has been reported."
        },
